t if i have to do it now or  lose it then i'm going to move for a  mistrial  let's bring back criminal defense  attorney taylor coss and terry austin  taylor we've heard long reports that  travis mcmichael called aubry a racial  slur after the shooting but the  prosecution didn't get it in before  resting what happened there  yeah i'm quite frankly i'm surprised  that that this testimony was not let in  especially when the individual who  allegedly said it is on the witness  stand uh you know this goes directly to  intent what's the frame of what's the  frame of mind of this individual if he's  using a racial slur does this really fit  into the alleged defense of self-defense  so i'm quite frankly stunned i  understand the concept that you know you  can't if you ask the question and he  says no i did not say that you're kind  of stuck with the answer but i still  don't understand why he's prevented from  asking a question i think the jury  should be able to hear this and evaluate  the credibility of that statement it  goes directly to intent it goes directly  to the core of the defense and i'm quite  frankly stunned that it was uh not  allowed in you know it was interesting  how that's being decided and wasn't  really ruled on before they arrested  terry after a motion by the defense  judge romsey ruled uh to admonish the  prosecutor for a controversial question  about the death penalty do you think  that was the right call  oh it definitely was the right call in  fact i was very surprised to hear  larissa oliveira say that question it  was just a witness who was a neighbor  and she asked have you ever been the  subject of a crime and then the very  next question was do you think someone  stealing should get the death penalty it  was offensive and i think laura hogue  made the right motion i don't think it  should have been a motion as we know  already that kevin goff did for a  mistrial the judge did the right thing  he said it was not necessary it was  irrelevant 