ent prosecutors offices across  the country that things like this can  happen and the good thing about these  types of investigations are that the  prosecutors work in tandem with the  attorneys for the alleged wrongfully  confused that wrongfully convicted and  that way there's a give and take there's  a sharing of evidence and this is how  justice happens you know there's not one  side withholding from the other trying  to get an edge up when you're working  together and really your only goal is  the truth great things like this can  happen and so it's a great day exactly  now terry does this exoneration and the  reasons for it create a civil claim for  aziz or islam's estate against the state  or fbi  you know what brian you are reading my  mind a wrongfully convicted individual  has two options they can sue under the  state's exoneration statute but there's  a limit there it's kept the number of  years multiplied by a certain amount of  money but they can also sue under the  constitution basically if they were  deprived of some sort of due process and  if that happens then there is an  unlimited amount of money that they can  actually  receive in that type of case and i think  they do have some constitutional claims  here some due process claims where they  can make and and make some damages here  it's interesting of course we'll follow  that case if that civil case does in  fact come up but right now these men are  exonerated one posthumously one still  alive like you said taylor good day for  all when we come back the latest in a  long list of lawsuits against actors and  producers of the ill-fated movie rust  right gloria allred says alec baldwin  was playing a game of russian roulette  at the time of the deadly shooting on  the movie sets all that and more after  the break  [Music]  welcome back to law and crime daily  famed attorney gloria allred announces  another lawsuit against actor alec  baldwin accusing him of playing russian  roulette on the film set