ned and you'd have to have  the same harm and you'd have to have the  same defendant so it's really going to  be a question of whether or not the same  laws the same facts and i think here we  do have that if these individuals are  all harmed in the same way and it really  will save on resources as far as  multiple trials might be concerned you  want to make sure that the state is  saving resources and not having multiple  lawsuits for something that really could  all be tried together so we'll see what  happens but if the numbers continue to  rise i think that is something that  they're going to have to consider to  keep the expenses down hey maybe we'll  see that gloria allred is representing  this class action suit as taylor i may  have been suggesting about her picking  up more cases well thank you both and  thank you for joining us here on law and  crime daily we'll see you next time as  we discuss justice in america  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

